# Sprint: Fix Catalogue Navigation Data Path

## Overview
**Goal**: Fix critical data path bugs from catalogue navigation click → products page. Ensure correct products are returned for each category.

**Current State**:
- Navigation uses `<a>` tag (full page reload)
- Slug resolution fails (using path instead of leaf slug)
- Empty catalogueKeys returns ALL products (wrong behavior)
- Products displayed don't match selected category

**Target State**:
- Client-side navigation with Next.js Link
- Correct slug resolution (leaf slug only)
- Empty keys returns NO products (correct behavior)
- Products match selected category
- Console logging for verification

---

## Critical Path Analysis

```
User Click (DetailSection.tsx)
    ↓
URL: /products/headphones/open-back
    ↓
page.tsx receives path = ["headphones", "open-back"]
    ↓
❌ BUG: slug = path.join("/") → "headphones/open-back" (wrong)
    ↓
❌ BUG: resolveSlugToId("headphones/open-back") → undefined
    ↓
❌ BUG: catalogueKeys = [] (empty)
    ↓
❌ BUG: getSelectedProducts([]) → returns ALL products (wrong)
    ↓
❌ ProductsGrid shows wrong products
```

---

## Regression Risk Assessment

**Code Areas at Risk**:
1. `app/components/layout/catalogue/details/DetailSection.tsx` - Navigation component
2. `app/(store)/products/[...category]/page.tsx` - Data flow coordinator
3. `sanity/lib/products/getSelectedProducts.ts` - Core product query
4. `data/catalogue.ts` - VFS utilities (read-only, but verify usage)

**Risk Mitigation**:
- All changes are additive or bug fixes
- No breaking changes to data structures
- Early return for edge cases

---

## Scope Contract 1: Fix Navigation (DetailSection.tsx)

**Objective**: Replace `<a>` tag with Next.js `Link` component for client-side navigation.

**Files to Modify**:
- `app/components/layout/catalogue/details/DetailSection.tsx`

**DoD - Layer 1 (Structure)**:
- [ ] Import `Link` from "next/link"
- [ ] Replace `<a>` element with `<Link>` component
- [ ] Keep `href={link.url}` prop unchanged
- [ ] Keep all existing className props

**DoD - Layer 2 (Layout)**:
- [ ] No visual changes to link appearance
- [ ] No changes to hover/active states
- [ ] Staggered animation delays preserved via CSS custom properties
- [ ] Group data attributes preserved for animation

**DoD - Layer 3 (Surface)**:
- [ ] Typography unchanged (text-body, text-secondary-300)
- [ ] Colors unchanged (hover:text-brand-200, active:text-brand-400)
- [ ] Spacing unchanged (pl-2)
- [ ] Transitions preserved (transition-colors)

**DoD - Layer 4 (Interaction)**:
- [ ] Client-side navigation works (no full page reload)
- [ ] Hover states work (text-brand-200)
- [ ] Active states work (text-brand-400)
- [ ] Keyboard navigation works
- [ ] Prefetching enabled by default

**Verification (Testing)**:
- [ ] Unit test: Link component renders correctly
- [ ] E2E test: Click catalogue item → no full page reload
- [ ] E2E test: Network tab shows no document requests
- [ ] Manual: Navigation feels instant (<100ms)

---

## Scope Contract 2: Fix Slug Resolution ([...category]/page.tsx)

**Objective**: Use leaf slug instead of joined path for catalogue resolution.

**Files to Modify**:
- `app/(store)/products/[...category]/page.tsx`

**DoD - Layer 1 (Structure)**:
- [ ] Change `const slug = path.join("/")` to `const slug = path[path.length - 1]`
- [ ] Add comment: "Use leaf slug, not full path"
- [ ] Keep `resolveSlugToId` call unchanged
- [ ] Keep `unrollDescendantKeys` call unchanged

**DoD - Layer 2 (Layout)**:
- [ ] Console logging added for verification:
  - [ ] Category path logged
  - [ ] Resolved ID logged
  - [ ] Catalogue keys count logged
  - [ ] Products count logged
  - [ ] Sample products logged

**DoD - Layer 3 (Surface)**:
- [ ] Console format:
  ```
  [Category] [path]
    ├─ Resolved ID: [id or "NOT FOUND"]
    ├─ Catalogue Keys: [count]
    ├─ Products Count: [count]
    └─ Sample Products: [names...]
  ```
- [ ] Only logs in development mode
- [ ] Clear visual hierarchy with tree characters

**DoD - Layer 4 (Interaction)**:
- [ ] Zero impact on production builds
- [ ] <5ms overhead for logging
- [ ] Errors in logging don't break page

**Verification (Testing)**:
- [ ] Unit test: URL /products/headphones/open-back resolves "open-back"
- [ ] Unit test: URL /products/accessories/earpads resolves "earpads"
- [ ] E2E test: Console shows correct resolved ID for each category
- [ ] Manual: All 22 categories resolve correctly

---

## Scope Contract 3: Fix Empty Keys Handling (getSelectedProducts.ts)

**Objective**: Return empty results when catalogueKeys is empty instead of ALL products.

**Files to Modify**:
- `sanity/lib/products/getSelectedProducts.ts`

**DoD - Layer 1 (Structure)**:
- [ ] Add early return guard at start of function
- [ ] Check: `if (!catalogueKeys || catalogueKeys.length === 0)`
- [ ] Return: `{ products: [], totalProductsCount: 0 }`
- [ ] Add comment: "Prevents returning ALL products when no category match"

**DoD - Layer 2 (Layout)**:
- [ ] Guard placed before any GROQ query assembly
- [ ] No database query executed when keys are empty
- [ ] Function returns immediately

**DoD - Layer 3 (Surface)**:
- [ ] Clear comment explaining the guard purpose
- [ ] No console logging in this function (keep clean)

**DoD - Layer 4 (Interaction)**:
- [ ] Zero impact when keys are present (normal flow)
- [ ] Zero impact on performance when keys present
- [ ] Fast failure when keys empty (<1ms)

**Verification (Testing)**:
- [ ] Unit test: Empty catalogueKeys returns `{ products: [], totalProductsCount: 0 }`
- [ ] Unit test: Null catalogueKeys returns empty result
- [ ] Unit test: Valid catalogueKeys returns filtered products
- [ ] E2E test: Invalid category URL shows "No products" message

---

